// while_loop.gopi
// Expected: 1 diagnostic (SEMANTIC) — "variable 'x' might not have been
// assigned a value", on the final print(x). A while loop's body might
// execute zero times (conservatively, even here, where the condition happens
// to be a literal `true`), so an assignment made only inside it is never
// considered definite afterward. The read/write of x INSIDE the loop body
// itself is fine — sequential assignment within the same block.

void main() {
    int x;
    while (true) {
        x = 5;
        print(x);
    }
    print(x);
}
